               <persName xml:id="n1" xml:lang="ar">الرملي, محمد بن احمد بن حمزة المنوفي المصري الانصاري شمس الدين</persName>
               <persName corresp="#n1" type="transliterated">al-Ramlī, Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Ḥamza al-Manūfī al-Miṣrī al-Anṣārī Šams al-Dīn</persName>
               <persName type="alt" xml:id="n2" xml:lang="ar">ابو العباس</persName>
               <persName corresp="#n2" type="transliterated">Abū al-'Abbās</persName>
               <floruit>10th / 16th century (d. 1595)<note>Prominent Šāfiʿī jurist. He was favourably disposed toward the Ṣūfīs. He was on familiar terms with the famous Egyptian Ṣūfī ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Šaʿrānī (d. 973/1565). Al-Ramlī's son-in-law Abū al-Mawāhib (d. 1037/1628) was a son of the Ṣūfī leader and poet Muḥammad al-Bakrī (d. 994/1586)</note>
               </floruit>
